## Running Locally with Docker

### Prerequisites

- Docker Desktop
- Node.js and npm
- Git

### 1. Clone the repository

git clone <https://github.com/devsadh-sde/ripple>
cd ripple

### 2. Configure the environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set a
local development PostgreSQL password.

### 3. Start backend services

docker compose up -d --build

This starts:
- PostgreSQL
- Event Service on localhost:8081
- Interaction Service on localhost:8082

### 4. Start the frontend

cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev

Open:

http://localhost:5173

## Example Workflow

1. Register an organizer account.
2. Log in and open the Presenter Dashboard.
3. Create an event.
4. Start the event.
5. Share its six-character join code.
6. Create and launch a poll.
7. Audience members join and submit votes.
8. View results as votes are recorded.
9. Close the poll.
10. End the event.

## API Examples

Event Service:

POST /api/auth/signup
POST /api/auth/login
GET  /api/auth/me
GET  /api/auth/csrf
POST /api/auth/logout

POST /api/events
GET  /api/events/{id}
GET  /api/events/code/{joinCode}
GET  /api/events/organizer/{organizerId}
POST /api/events/{id}/start
POST /api/events/{id}/end

Interaction Service:

POST /api/polls
GET  /api/polls/event/{eventId}
GET  /api/polls/event/{eventId}/live
POST /api/polls/{id}/start
POST /api/polls/{id}/close
POST /api/polls/{id}/votes
GET  /api/polls/{id}/results

## Security

Ripple implements:
- BCrypt password hashing
- Server-managed organizer sessions
- Session-based event ownership verification
- Authorization checks for poll management
- CSRF token validation for organizer operations

Security integration is intended for local development
and portfolio demonstration.

Production deployment requires additional hardening,
including HTTPS, secure service-to-service authentication,
session management, and security review.

